<title>FRANCE: SocGen sells two pct of stock,610 Fr/shr.</title>
<headline>SocGen sells two pct of stock,610 Fr/shr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Societe Generale said on Tuesday broker SGE Delehaye had sold two million SocGen treasury stock shares, or 2.2 percent of SocGen capital, at 610 francs per share.  </p>
<p>&quot;The transaction is part of the plan to acquire Credit de Nord,&quot; it said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>Societe Generale announced on January 9 that it and Paribas had agreed to start talks on a speedy acquisition by SocGen of Paribas bank unit Credit du Nord for 2.2 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
